'''Roar''' instills fear in up to 6{{vn|plain}} nearby enemies, causing them to flee and be set off balance. This ability also grants a stack of Blood Hunger which further empowers [[ON:Gnash|Gnash]] [[Online:Rending Claws|Rending Claws]] and up to 12 nearby allies can activate the {{ESO Synergy Link|Feeding Frenzy}} [[Online:Synergy|synergy]]. When activated it will increase damage and apply [[Online:Minor Force|Minor Force]] for 30 seconds. Having this ability slotted will grant you [[Online:Major Prophecy|Major Prophecy]] and [[Online:Major Savagery|Savagery]], increasing your {{ESO Weapon Critical Link}} and {{ESO Spell Critical Link}}.

'''Ferocious Roar''' grants you and your allies [[ON:Major Courage|Major Courage]] and also allows you to use your own Feeding Frenzy synergy.

The '''Deafening Roar''' morph will apply [[Online:Major Cowardice|Major Cowardice]] and [[Online:Major Maim|Maim]] debuffs to enemies, and converts your slot bonuses to [[Online:Major Evasion|Major Evasion]] and [[Online:Minor Protection|Minor Protection]]. Using this morph will also turn the [[ON:Gnash|Gnash]] ability into a [[Online:taunt|taunt]] while Bracing.
{{NewLeft}}

== Notes ==
* The passive effects of '''Roar''' apply even when the ability is slotted on an active, non-Werewolf skill bar.
* '''Deafening Roar''' replaced the ability Rousing Roar in [[ON:Patch/4.1.5|Update 19]] which previously increased yours and your allies {{ESO Weapon Damage Link}}.
* The '''Terrified''' debuff uses the following icon: {{icon|misc|Draining Poison}}
